 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "It is a busy afternoon of prep in the kitchen, and Chef Barinov is on the warpath. He catches Senya, who cooks the meat, standing around. Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сеня, почему ты стоишь без дела?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я жду нужные специи для мяса.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ждёшь, пока гном насыпет корицу?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф, я всё делаю быстро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Тогда работай быстрее и не стой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "И всегда убирай за собой стол.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф, говорите немного тише, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Не надо учить меня дисциплине!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы просто очень стараемся для вас.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "На моей кухне должен быть идеальный порядок.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы сейчас же всё уберём, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Спокойнее, я проверю каждое блюдо лично.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "One barked order at a time.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Сеня, почему ты стоишь без дела?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Senya, why are you standing doing nothing?' To say 'idle', Russian says ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "без",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "дела",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", which means 'without business'. Barinov uses an informal 'you' with his cook, seen in the verb ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "стоишь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Я жду нужные специи для мяса.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am waiting for the needed spices for the meat.' Russian says ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "жду",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "нужные",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "специи",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " without 'for' after 'wait'. The term for meat, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "мяса",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", takes a different ending after 'for'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты ждёшь, пока гном насыпет корицу?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you waiting until a gnome sprinkles cinnamon?' We will analyze the dialogue: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Ты",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "ждёшь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " matches Senya's 'I wait'. The word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "пока",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means 'until' here, and the gnome is Barinov's sarcastic picture of how slow Senya is.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф, я всё делаю быстро.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, I do everything quickly.' We will focus on the dialogue: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "всё",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means 'everything' and is a very common small word. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "быстро",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means 'quickly'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "Тогда работай быстрее и не стой.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Then work faster and do not stand around.' Change the ending of 'quickly' and it becomes ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "быстрее",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning 'faster'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "работай",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the command 'work!' and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "стой",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is 'do not stand'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "И всегда убирай за собой стол.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And always clean up your table.' Let's look at the words: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "всегда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " means 'always'. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "за",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "barinov",
   "t": "собой",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " expresses cleaning up 'after yourself', phrased as 'behind yourself'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф, говорите немного тише, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Chef, please speak a bit quieter.' Senya uses the polite 'you' form in ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "говорите",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " because he is talking to the chef. ",
   "gap": 0.25
